- A redundant architecture ensures that:
	➢ No single failure can bring the system down (no single point of failure, or SPOF).
	➢ Service continuity is preserved through failover mechanisms.
	➢ Maintenance or upgrades can occur without service interruption.
	➢ The system can detect, isolate, and recover from faults automatically.
	
- Redundancy embodies the principle “design for failure” , assuming that every hardware, software, and network element will eventually fail

- 3dna 	
	- Hardware Redundancy (NIC Bonding, Dual PSUs) 
	- Network Redundancy (Duplicate paths, HSRP, LACP, ECMP Routing) 
	- Data Redundancy (DB Replication) 
